{"id": "EUVD-2026-108737", "enisaUuid": "37c43141-034b-3791-9df2-1ef8c52aa7c8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipv4: do not warn on route notification size race\n\nCommit 680aea08e78c (\"net: ipv4: Emit notification when fib hardware\nflags are changed\") added asynchronous route notifications for hardware\nflag changes.\n\nfib_alias_hw_flags_set() sizes the skb with fib_nlmsg_size() and later\nfills it with fib_dump_info() while holding only RCU.  With nexthop\ncompatibility mode enabled, a concurrent replacement can grow the group\nbetween these independent snapshots.  fib_dump_info() can then\nlegitimately return -EMSGSIZE, so the warning does not prove a sizing bug.\n\nRemove the warning.  The existing error path still frees the skb and\nreports the error to listeners.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:23:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:23:14", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/088ba80eef85fa7a5ad8f9e7c82b403c99242b56", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/78a1cf5c54b2f795c81fedb530755a8d01cc84f0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7dfa7ca97f3ac46353edd4cc44f7733758e4535b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/221ef5e1e44a044790f0f54e6aa237883f475a4d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e02a5b6588161673ef75a4bc5cdfb62bd493374d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99071"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "15f54dbd-df60-3a14-9c44-3dae20485d21", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "1eaa80fd-05d4-3a0f-a3a1-1ea3da63789d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "680aea08e78c003292415518ad270bc20f9c80b1 <221ef5e1e44a044790f0f54e6aa237883f475a4d"}, {"id": "2265a2a8-d5c2-3a44-bdc8-5c22ffc3deb9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "680aea08e78c003292415518ad270bc20f9c80b1 <088ba80eef85fa7a5ad8f9e7c82b403c99242b56"}, {"id": "5a5dee2a-e974-3ce9-bce0-5266c60ab6cd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "680aea08e78c003292415518ad270bc20f9c80b1 <e02a5b6588161673ef75a4bc5cdfb62bd493374d"}, {"id": "5c8cd941-a217-3cee-8986-8177b1a96e9b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "97e7e933-0113-3b4c-8fa7-ac6b847e709f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "9cd8bb0c-e88f-33f9-9f0c-a280379a2994", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "680aea08e78c003292415518ad270bc20f9c80b1 <78a1cf5c54b2f795c81fedb530755a8d01cc84f0"}, {"id": "9fe65726-7816-3f69-83df-df7ad794724c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "db0f0dca-0047-3321-9c40-3e4bd9038699", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "680aea08e78c003292415518ad270bc20f9c80b1 <7dfa7ca97f3ac46353edd4cc44f7733758e4535b"}, {"id": "f59cf1d4-7884-3640-a6c5-cdf88755d9f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.12"}, {"id": "f6e606d2-a357-3578-a5c4-da0f030a7606", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "fcdd05cb-341c-3bd1-8d6d-7b7217ff3806", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4e9941e1-0650-36d9-9f0c-f12ed35d5582", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}